    "design_summary": "The case presents a time-resolved X-ray absorption spectroscopy (trXAS) experiment on a cuprate ladder material. The player controls the photon energy (omega) and observes the fitted XAS intensity. Two hidden regimes are compared: the equilibrium (pre-pump) state and a transient state at 0.4 ps after optical excitation. The underlying spectral model is a sum of three Lorentzian peaks plus a linear background, with different fit parameters in each regime. The player must infer how the intensity-energy relationship changes between the two regimes.",
